# ************************************
#   Comments + Keyword Clarification

#    Anton, Calculus, 0.1.10a
# ************************************
# DESCRIPTION
# Determine the domain and range of f(x) = sqrt(A - x)

# ENDDESCRIPTION
## DBsubject('Calculus')
## DBchapter('Before Calculus')
## DBsection('Functions')
## KEYWORDS('Functions', 'Domain', 'Range')
## TitleText1('Calculus')
## EditionText1('9')
## AuthorText1('Anton')
## Section1('0.1')
## Problem1('10a')
## Author('')
## Institution('John Wiley & Sons')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Numeric");
#****************************************************
#  Create function of form sqrt(A^2 - x^2)
#****************************************************
$A    = random(1, 30);
$Func = Formula("sqrt($A - x)");
#*************************************************************************************
#                               Answers

#   For sq. root, want $A - x >= 0, or x <= $A. As an interval, domain is (-inf,$A]
#   For sq. root, range is [0,inf)
#*************************************************************************************
Context("Interval");
$Domain = Compute("(-inf,$A]");
$Range  = Compute("[0,inf)");
#*******************
#   Display stuff
#*******************
Context("Numeric")->variables->add(y => 'Real');
$Ysqr = Formula("$A^2 - x^2")->reduce;
$Xsqr = Formula("$A^2 - y^2")->reduce;
$XofY = Formula("sqrt($A^2 - y^2)")->reduce;

BEGIN_PGML
Find the domain and range of the function [`f(x) = [$Func] `]. Express each in
interval notation.

a) Domain: [_]{$Domain}

b) Range: [_]{$Range}

[@ helpLink('interval') @]*
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
For a square root function such as [` f(x) = [$Func] `], the domain is restricted to
all values of [` x `] that do not produce a negative value inside the radical.
Therefore, the domain of this function includes all real values of [` x`] such that 
[` [$A] - x \ge 0 `], or [` x \le [$A] `]. Expressed in interval form, this is
[` [$Domain] `].

By the definition of the square root, the result is strictly nonnegative. Therefore, 
[` f(x) \ge 0 `]. Expressed in interval form, this is [` [$Range] `].  
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
